# Files excluded from Semgrep scanning.
#
# These files contain patterns that Semgrep flags as security issues but which
# are intentional, operator-controlled, and already covered by gosec (#nosec),
# CodeQL, and SonarCloud (NOSONAR) with proper per-tool suppressions.
# Semgrep's inline `// nosemgrep` comment suppression is incompatible with the
# co-located gosec `// #nosec` directives that these same lines require, because
# both tools require their own directive to appear first in the comment.

# All Go test files — hardcoded test credentials (JWT keys, AWS key IDs, bcrypt
# hashes, OAuth tokens), cookies without Secure/HttpOnly, raw ResponseWriter
# writes, and exec/SQL calls in test helpers are intentional test fixtures, not
# production vulnerabilities. Real security coverage for these patterns is
# provided by CodeQL and gosec on the production code paths.
*_test.go

# InsecureSkipVerify=true — an explicit operator opt-in, guarded by a config
# flag (insecure_skip_verify: true) and a loud WARNING log at startup.
# Suppressed by // #nosec G402 for gosec; covered by CodeQL + SonarCloud.
internal/audit/siem/forwarder.go
internal/evidencesink/webhook.go
internal/notifychan/webhook.go
internal/storage/remote/client.go

# MySQL dynamic-credential DDL (CREATE USER, DROP USER) — MySQL DDL cannot use
# parameterized query placeholders; values are validated by assertSafeUsername
# ([a-z0-9_]@%) before interpolation, and passwords come from randString (no
# quoting-sensitive characters). Suppressed by //nolint:gosec for gosec;
# covered by CodeQL + SonarCloud NOSONAR. nosemgrep inline comments present
# but ineffective (tool-compatibility constraint documented in the file header).
internal/dynamic/mysql.go

# Cookie Secure/HttpOnly attributes — Secure is threaded from the runtime TLS
# config (cfg.Server.HTTP.TLS.Enabled), not statically false; HttpOnly:false
# is intentional for the CSRF double-submit cookie pattern.
# Suppressed by // #nosec G124 for gosec; covered by CodeQL + SonarCloud.
server/middleware/session_cookie.go

# SONAR_TOKEN — a GitHub Actions ${{ secrets.SONAR_TOKEN }} reference, not a
# plaintext SonarQube API key. The detected-sonarqube-docs-api-key rule is a
# false positive triggered by the env-var name pattern.
.github/workflows/sonarcloud.yml
